  "question": {
    "text": "A block of mass <math><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo></math> lying on a smooth horizontal surface, is attached to a spring (of negligible mass) of spring constant <math><mi>k</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The other end of the spring is fixed, as shown in the figure. The block is initially at rest in its equilibrium position. If now the block is pulled with a constant force <math><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the maximum speed of the block is:<br /><br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0126_1cf6379b4491.png\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>",
